  "period_end": "2026-06-30",
  "title": "A place to try the models",
  "summary": "June made more kinds of generation easier to try, while giving builders clearer model information and people more ways to track and earn Pollen.\n\nThe standalone Playground brought image, video, text, and audio generation into one app. Websim gained a prompt-and-preview workspace, and both fit more cleanly inside /play. A live model catalog now supplies capabilities and pricing across the SDK and model pages.\n\nNew options spanned Claude, Kimi, MiniMax, Mercury, Ideogram, NanoBanana, Wan, and Pruna. Audio grew beyond speech with reference-guided music, Stable Audio 3, and sound effects. Explicit video resolution models made 1080p a choice rather than a hopeful parameter.\n\nEnter added transaction history and brought filtered usage, transactions, and app earnings together in Activity. Quests gained a public catalog, claimable rewards, and a dashboard showing what people have earned and claimed.\n\nNew apps kept joining the catalog as dead links were pruned. Builders also gained public app stats and an OpenAPI spec. By month’s end, invited owners could register OpenAI-compatible text endpoints in Enter and publish them as community models.",
